{
  "an9.34:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 9.34 ",
  "an9.34:0.2": "4. The Great Chapter ",
  "an9.34:0.3": "Extinguishment is Bliss ",
  "an9.34:1.1": "At one time Venerable Sāriputta was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "an9.34:1.2": "There he addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an9.34:1.3": "“Reverends, extinguishment is bliss! ",
  "an9.34:1.4": "Extinguishment is bliss!” ",
  "an9.34:1.5": "When he said this, Venerable Udāyī said to him, ",
  "an9.34:1.6": "“But Reverend Sāriputta, what’s blissful about it, since nothing is felt?” ",
  "an9.34:1.7": "“The fact that nothing is felt is precisely what’s blissful about it. ",
  "an9.34:1.8": "Reverend, there are these five kinds of sensual stimulation. ",
  "an9.34:1.9": "What five? ",
  "an9.34:1.10": "Sights known by the eye, which are likable, desirable, agreeable, pleasant, sensual, and arousing. ",
  "an9.34:1.11": "Sounds known by the ear … ",
  "an9.34:1.12": "Smells known by the nose … ",
  "an9.34:1.13": "Tastes known by the tongue … ",
  "an9.34:1.14": "Touches known by the body, which are likable, desirable, agreeable, pleasant, sensual, and arousing. ",
  "an9.34:1.15": "These are the five kinds of sensual stimulation. ",
  "an9.34:1.16": "The pleasure and happiness that arise from these five kinds of sensual stimulation is called sensual pleasure. ",
  "an9.34:2.1": "First, take a mendicant who, quite secluded from sensual pleasures … enters and remains in the first absorption. ",
